<div class="page-header"><h1 class="page-header__title">Contact and Support</h1><p class="page-header__subtitle">HelloDeploy is run by <%= legalOperator %>. Support is best-effort by email.</p></div>
<div class="card prose"><div class="card__body">
  <h2>Before you write</h2>
  <p>Most questions are answered in the <a href="/docs">documentation</a>, the <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">troubleshooting guide</a>, and the <a href="/docs/faq">FAQ</a>.</p>

  <h2>Email us</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:<%= legalContactEmail %>"><%= legalContactEmail %></a></p>
  <p>Include your account email, the project name, and the deployment number if a deployment failed. We reply as soon as we can, but there is no guaranteed response time during the pilot.</p>
  <aside class="docs-guide-note" role="note"><strong>Never send secrets</strong><p>Do not include passwords, API keys, tokens, deploy hook URLs, or environment variable values. Remove them from any log or screenshot you share. HelloDeploy will never ask for your password.</p></aside>

  <h2>Use this address for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Help with deployments and your account</li>
    <li>Privacy requests, such as access, correction, or deletion (see the <a href="/privacy#your-rights">Privacy Policy</a>)</li>
    <li>Appeals of suspensions (see the <a href="/acceptable-use#appeals">Acceptable Use Policy</a>) and account closure if you cannot sign in. Signed-in users can request closure from their <a href="/account#close-account">Account page</a>.</li>
    <li>Abuse and copyright reports (see the <a href="/copyright">Copyright Policy</a>)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security vulnerabilities</h2>
  <p>Report vulnerabilities privately as described in the <a href="/security">Security Policy</a>. Send a short summary first, without exploit details or other people&rsquo;s data.</p>
</div></div>
